## Problem
`c2c whoami --relay` reports registered_unreachable with: relay lease alive but no live connector bridge — inbound relay traffic will not reach this broker. Concurrently a long-lived `c2c relay connect` process can exist on the host (observed multi-hour ELAPSED) while connector last sync is ~1.4d. Operators cannot tell whether to restart connect, re-register, or ignore.

## Expected
- Clear liveness: process presence != bridge health
- Actionable remediation in whoami/status (restart connect, check token, check socket)
- Self-heal or loud fail if connect is wedged
- last_sync should update when connect is actually healthy

## Actual
Lease alive + connect PID present + last sync 1.4d + inbound relay unreliable. Status language is partial but not enough to drive recovery.

## Suggested fix
Connector heartbeat into broker status; whoami distinguishes (no process | process dead socket | process alive not authenticated | bridge ok); optional watchdog to restart wedged connect.